#!/usr/bin/env bash
# UserPromptSubmit hook (thesis repo only): keeps the adversarial ICLR-spotlight
# reviewer in play WITHOUT Lokesh having to ask for it (standing request,
# 2026-07-22). Emits a one-line reminder when the prompt looks like a research
# decision; silent otherwise so it never taxes mechanical turns.
#
# Contract: stdin = JSON event payload; stdout = context injected for the model.
# Must stay <1s on the no-op path.
set -uo pipefail

payload="$(cat 2>/dev/null || true)"

# Only for the thesis repo.
case "${PWD:-}" in
  *Research/LiteratureSurvey*) ;;
  *) exit 0 ;;
esac

# Cheap keyword screen over the prompt text (no jq dependency).
# NOTE (2026-07-24): the pure-presentation triggers (paper/present/report) were
# removed so authoring work is not auto-nagged. Genuine research-decision keywords
# still fire; anything narrower is summoned on demand with the `/critic` command
# (Claude) or `just critic` (pi).
prompt="$(printf '%s' "$payload" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')"
case "$prompt" in
  *experiment*|*baseline*|*benchmark*|*ablation*|*claim*|*result*|*metric*|\
  *scenario*|*seed*|*iclr*|*spotlight*|*novel*|\
  *contribution*|*evaluat*|*sufficient*|*enough*|*conclude*|*shows*|*proves*|\
  *significan*|*compare*|*sota*|*state-of-the-art*|*reviewer*)
    cat <<'EOF'
[research-gate] This turn touches a research decision. Per Lokesh's standing
requests, invoke the `research` skill and run its gate BEFORE acting on or
reporting the decision:
  1. theorist (research/references/theorist.md) — what existing theory predicts
     this outcome, or the NOVEL falsifiable hypothesis the experiment will
     prove/disprove (novelty checked against the literature graph + the
     hypothesis ledger). No hypothesis => not a severe test => send it back.
  2. critic (research/references/critic.md) — adversarial ICLR-spotlight review
     as a subagent; for an experiment plan this is a HARD GATE (no compute until
     cleared as a severe test whose failure is as informative as its success).
Report the hypothesis, the top objections, and their cost to fix. Do not
suppress an inconvenient critique. (To summon this gate yourself at any time:
`/critic` in Claude, `just critic` in pi.)
EOF
    ;;
esac
exit 0
